​We checked into Hotel Parth Residence around 8:00–9:00 PM for a brief stay. Having checked online, the tariff for two rooms (accommodating four guests) was hovering around ₹3,500. While the front desk initially quoted a higher rate, they were courteous enough to negotiate, ultimately honoring a price slightly lower than the online rate.

​Here is a comprehensive breakdown of our experience, highlighting the commendable aspects and the areas that require urgent attention:

​The Positives (What Worked)
​Flexible Pricing: The management was accommodating regarding the room tariff, providing us with a budget-friendly deal.

​Wholesome Dinner: We ordered two Veg Royal Thalis, and the quantity was highly satisfactory—one thali was easily sufficient for two people. It featured rice, a paneer dish, a mushroom curry, and dal. The food had a comforting, wholesome, home-cooked quality to it and wasn''t overly spiced.

​Decent Room Space: The rooms and bathrooms were visually decent and clean. Basic amenities like an electric kettle for tea and coffee were readily available.

​The Negatives (The Pitfalls)

​Malfunctioning Amenities: Despite the decent aesthetics, functionality was lacking. The water heaters (geysers) in both assigned rooms were completely broken. Additionally, the air conditioning was subpar; even after lowering the temperature to the minimum, the cooling efficiency remained underwhelming. There was also no mini-fridge provided.

​A Painfully Sluggish Elevator: The hotel''s elevator is arguably its biggest drawback. It operates on an agonizingly slow timeline, taking an eternity to open and close. The call buttons are unresponsive, requiring multiple presses to register. To make matters worse, the lift stalled briefly mid-floor during our stay, though thankfully the power backup kicked in to rescue us.

​Cramped Parking: While basement parking is advertised, it is incredibly tight, barely accommodating 5 to 6 vehicles. If you arrive late, you will likely be forced to park your car outside on the street.

​Lackluster Breakfast & No Complimentary Water: The inclusive breakfast spread was incredibly limited, offering only sandwiches, cornflakes, and parathas served with curd and pickle. Tea was strictly on-demand. Furthermore, packaged water bottles were fully chargeable, with zero complimentary bottles provided with breakfast (only basic RO water was free).

​Infrastructure & Safety Issues: On the morning of our check-out, a light shower exposed structural flaws. Rainwater was leaking heavily onto the staircase leading to the basement, rendering the steps dangerously slippery—a severe safety hazard in case of an emergency evacuation.

​Final Verdict
​Rating: 3 / 5 (Mediocre)
Hotel Parth Residence is neither exceptionally good nor terribly bad. It sits squarely in the average category. It serves as a passable, pocket-friendly pitstop if you only need a place to sleep and a decent meal. However, until they overhaul their erratic elevator, fix the plumbing, and address the rainwater seepage, do not expect a seamless experience
