I recently had the opportunity, or rather, the misfortune, of hosting a reception party at Sonia Palace, a venue known for providing banquet hall and reception party services. Regrettably, my experience was far from what I had hoped for, and it is with a heavy heart that I share this comprehensive review.

To begin with, the service at Sonia Palace was nothing short of pathetic. From the moment we arrived, it was evident that the staff was lacking in both quantity and efficiency. The venue seemed to be understaffed, resulting in a noticeable shortage of personnel to assist guests. This deficiency manifested in various aspects throughout the event, leaving a lasting impression of incompetence.

One glaring issue was the lack of service staff, commonly referred to as "boys" in event management. Their scarcity meant that guests were left unattended, causing frustration and inconvenience. It was disheartening to witness the overwhelmed existing staff struggling to meet the demands of the occasion. This not only affected the overall ambiance but also led to prolonged waiting times for basic services.

Parking, a seemingly straightforward aspect of event planning, turned out to be another significant shortcoming at Sonia Palace. The lack of proper parking facilities created chaos as guests scrambled to find suitable spaces for their vehicles. This oversight in logistical planning not only inconvenienced attendees but also reflected a lack of attention to detail and consideration for the overall guest experience.

The management of Sonia Palace left much to be desired. A well-run event venue requires meticulous planning, coordination, and execution. Unfortunately, Sonia Palace fell short on all these fronts. The evident lack of coordination among the staff, coupled with a seemingly disorganized approach to managing events, contributed to the overall disappointment.

Despite these shortcomings, it''s important to acknowledge any positive aspects. The venue itself had potential with its aesthetically pleasing banquet hall. However, the lackluster service overshadowed any redeeming qualities the physical space might have had. A well-designed venue loses its charm when the service and management fail to meet even the most basic expectations.

In conclusion, my experience at Sonia Palace was marred by poor service, inefficient management, and logistical oversights. The shortage of staff, slow-paced work, and the absence of proper parking facilities significantly impacted the overall enjoyment of the event. In light of these issues, a 1.5-star rating seems appropriate, reflecting the disappointment and frustration that defined my time at Sonia Palace. It is my hope that this review serves as constructive feedback for the management to address these issues and improve the quality of service for future patrons.', '2 years ago', 'GOOGLE_MAPS', '2026-09-22 13:08:54.056063+05:30') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
