1. For the premium price of ₹3,000 a night, you get the exclusive privilege of acting as your own porter, because absolutely no staff will appear to help you haul your luggage from the car.

2. They maximize your physical fitness by keeping the elevator strictly "under maintenance," ensuring you get a full-body workout dragging those heavy bags up the stairs yourself.

3. Don''t let the "No Smoking" signs fool you; they are purely aesthetic, as the hotel generously perfumes the entire lobby and corridors with the heavy, stale stench of cigarette smoke.

4. The bed linens come pre-personalized with a lovely brown/red mystery stain, completely saving you from the boring sterility of clean sheets.

5. When politely asked to swap out the stained linen, the staff displayed lightning-fast urgency, taking a swift 30 minutes just to hand over a basic sheet change.

6. The bedroom boasts a custom, avant-garde peeling wallpaper installation behind the headboard that is physically hanging on for dear life.

7. The media console area features a high-tech "bird''s nest" design, beautifully showcasing exposed, loose wires dangling casually everywhere.

8. For ₹3,000, they completely dispense with modern bathroom fixtures, treating you instead to a vintage blue plastic bucket and red mug setup.

9. The washbasin arrives pre-seasoned with dark specks and debris, ensuring you know the staff didn''t waste an ounce of energy cleaning it before your arrival.

10. If you want to spend thousands to experience absolute staff abandonment, zero maintenance, and total hygiene failures, this place is an absolute masterclass.', '2 months ago', 'GOOGLE_MAPS', '2026-09-22 13:28:37.614814+05:30') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
